<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Twenty-first Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">1077 BCE – 943 BCE (approx.) · capital Tanis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The kings of Tanis who ruled northern Egypt after the New Kingdom, sharing the country with the priests of Amun at Thebes.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-xi">Ramesses XI</a> around 1077 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smendes">Smendes</a>, who had governed the north from the Delta, became king and founded the Twenty-first Dynasty. The capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanis">Tanis</a> in the north-eastern Delta, built largely from monuments carried from the abandoned Ramesside capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pi-ramesses">Pi-Ramesses</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Tanite kings ruled Lower and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-egypt">Middle Egypt</a>, while the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/theocracy-of-amun-at-thebes">Theocracy of Amun at Thebes</a> governed the south with family ties to them. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanis">Tanis</a> was laid out as a northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a> with a great temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a>. The intact royal tombs found there by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-montet">Pierre Montet</a> in 1939 to 1940 include the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coffin and gold mask of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/psusennes-i">Psusennes I</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siamun">Siamun</a> probably campaigned in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/philistine-pentapolis">Philistia</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osorkon-the-elder">Osorkon the Elder</a> was a Libyan.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 943 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shoshenq-i">Sheshonq I</a>, a Libyan chief of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/meshwesh">Meshwesh</a> and relative by marriage of the last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/psusennes-ii">Psusennes II</a>, succeeded peacefully and founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/twenty-second-dynasty-of-egypt">Twenty-second Dynasty of Egypt</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/twenty-first-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Twenty-first Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="482"><figcaption>Image: Tjflex2 or (Craig Elliott) · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Psusennes_I%27s_Funerary_Mask_in_2012.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1077 BCE – 943 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tanis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Smendes, Psusennes I, Siamun</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Twenty-first Dynasty, Tanite Dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1010&amp;focus=twenty-first-dynasty-of-egypt" aria-label="Twenty-first Dynasty of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5505 1048 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Twenty-first Dynasty of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5825 1304L5863 1489M5825 1304L5817 1318M5825 1304L5863 1488"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5863 1489h0M5817 1318h0M5863 1488h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5825 1304h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5825 1304h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tanis. <a href="/atlas?year=-1010&amp;focus=twenty-first-dynasty-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
